\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From reflected observables to relativistic fields}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The [reflection-positive pairing](fdip-007M) turns positive-time
observables into a Hilbert space after its null vectors are removed.
For the continuum state, \ref{fdip-00I8} also controls the
dependence on time and \ref{fdip-00IE} removes persistent correlations
at large separation. How do these facts give local quantum field
operators and a positive-energy action of spacetime symmetries?
The applicable reconstruction theorem is
\citet{Theorem 2.6, pp. 290-291}{frohlich1974verification}.}
